course: dictionary
lesson: 5193
title: Names with capital letters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Jacob is a proper noun. A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or thing, so it always starts with a capital letter. Jacob is a first name, so you write Jacob, not jacob.
explain: «Isaac's son Jacob tricked his twin Esau out of his birthright and blessing.» Jacob is a person in this story, and the capital J tells you it is his name. Words like son and twin are clues that Jacob is a boy or a man.
explain: Short forms of names are often friendlier. «Jake» and «Jakey» are short forms of Jacob, and people use them as nicknames. A nickname is not a person's full name, but it still starts with a capital letter.
fact: Jacob is a proper noun: it names one particular person, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: Jacob is a boy's or man's first name, and it is common in English-speaking countries.
fact: In the Bible, Jacob is the son of Isaac and the father of twelve sons, including Joseph.
fact: «Jake» and «Jakey» are short forms of Jacob that people use as friendly nicknames.
fact: «Jacob's ladder» is a toy, and it is also the name for a rope ladder. The J is a capital because it is part of a name.
exercise: «Jake and I play football at break.» Jake is a short form of which name? | Esau | Isaac | Joseph | *Jacob
exercise: Which sentence uses the name correctly? | jacob kicked the ball to me. | *Jacob kicked the ball to me. | Ball kicked jacob to me.
exercise: Why does «Jacob's ladder» start with a capital J? | *Because Jacob is a name, a proper noun | Because it is a food | Because it is at the start of a sentence | Because it is a long word
test: Jacob is a boy's first name. What kind of noun is it? | Common noun | Verb | *Proper noun | Adjective
test: Which short form of Jacob is a friendly nickname? | *Jake | Jacket | Jug | Jam
exam: «Years later Esau ran to meet Jacob and hugged him instead of taking revenge.» Why does Jacob start with a capital letter? | Because it is a happy word | Because it is the first word of the sentence | Because it is a long word | *Because it is a name of a particular person
